          "title": "GameSmith: Scaling Zero-Sum Self-Play with Synthesised Games",
          "title_zh": "GameSmith：用合成游戏扩展零和自博弈",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2610.13995v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2610.13995",
          "summary": "GameSmith uses an LLM to synthesize games inside fixed templates, verifies each by seed-paired replay and an independent re-implementation, and expands them into 26 new games in 29 families and 336 variants from three SPIRAL templates. The student is distilled from a larger Qwen3-32B teacher's self-play and then trained with self-play RL using CRAB, an advantage estimator defined on every variant; on Qwen3-4B-Base distillation raises the 13-benchmark mean pass@1 from 45.5 to 62.5 and self-play with CRAB reaches 64.9, above the three original games at the same budget.",
