          "title": "What Must a World Model Distinguish for Planning?",
          "title_zh": "世界模型为规划必须区分什么？",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2609.33030v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.33030",
          "summary": "The paper formalizes a hierarchy of mechanism, response, and decision sufficiency to argue that what a world model must preserve depends on the planning query, the candidate set, and the planner, and studies these effects in a collision system, nonlinear dynamics, and robotic planning. Query-conditioned models that jointly generate actions and outcomes achieve lower regret on seen objectives but lose most of that advantage on unseen ones, motivating a modular design where the query determines where to look and an action-conditioned model predicts what happens.",
