          "title_zh": "基于内外信息交互的模型感知数据选择",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2609.33010v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.33010",
          "summary": "The authors observe a rank equilibrium in which hidden-state rank follows a U-shape across layers while weight rank follows an inverted U, and interpret intermediate activations as carrying mainly what the weights cannot supply. Building on this, they propose CAP, a counterfactual data selection method that reports 35.4% greater average improvement over the base model than the strongest baseline across math, code, and science, and matches or beats full-pool training with only 10% of the data on math and science.",
