          "title": "The Epistemics of Agent Memory: Measuring, and Governing, the Consolidation Decision in Long-Horizon LLM Agents",
          "title_zh": "智能体记忆的认识论：度量与治理长程 LLM 智能体的整合决策",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2609.33013v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.33013",
          "summary": "This four-phase research program studies how long-horizon LLM agents decide what to keep, compress, abstract into reusable skills, or forget, moving from learned episodic boundaries and promotion policies to the ConsolidationBench benchmark and a governed-consolidation phase with poison-resistance, reversibility, and auditability guarantees. It reports a verified +22.7% task-success gain with 7x compression, shows governance quality is statistically distinct from consolidation quality (r-squared = 0.43), and finds that the quality score does not predict real transfer accuracy.",
