          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.33016",
          "summary": "The paper introduces Relative Generalization Invariance (RGI), the invariance across models of the validation-loss difference between any two tokens, and shows it approximately holds across a wide range of optimizers and moderate architectural variations but not when the training data stream changes. The authors show RGI is not explained by neural tangent kernel or mean-field regimes alone and prove it can emerge in an overparameterized quadratic model.",
