          "summary": "The authors build an evaluation that scores trust and task completion on the same runs in a simulated world of businesses with their own websites, inboxes, and phone lines, pairing every trap with a matched control where acting is correct. Wajo's assistant Fo completes 71% of errands and keeps the user's trust on 94% of trap runs, versus 50-64% completion and 59-75% trust for base models on three foundation models and 42% completion and 74% trust for OpenClaw on shared errands.",
